/--------------------------------------------------------------------
/ TELEMAC2D steering file generated by hydromate for case 'ering'
/ regime: steady
/ revised v2 for improved numerical robustness while preserving:
/   - TURBULENCE MODEL : 3 and existing k-epsilon accuracy settings
/   - SCHEME FOR ADVECTION OF VELOCITIES : 14
/   - linear-compatible finite element discretization for distributive scheme 14
/--------------------------------------------------------------------
TITLE : 'ering steady - stable numerics v2'
/
/ INPUT / OUTPUT FILES
GEOMETRY FILE : geometry.slf
BOUNDARY CONDITIONS FILE : boundaries.cli
RESULTS FILE : r2d.slf
MASS-BALANCE : YES
VARIABLES FOR GRAPHIC PRINTOUTS : 'U,V,S,B,H,M,Q,F,K,E'
PRINTING CUMULATED FLOWRATES : YES
/
/ TIME
/ Conservative start step and Courant target for wetting/drying + k-epsilon.
TIME STEP : 0.25
VARIABLE TIME-STEP : YES
DESIRED COURANT NUMBER : 0.30
DURATION : 5000.0
/ Keep roughly the same physical printout interval as the original 1 s / 500 steps.
GRAPHIC PRINTOUT PERIOD : 2000
LISTING PRINTOUT PERIOD : 2000
/
/ NUMERICS (finite elements)
ADVECTION : YES
TREATMENT OF THE LINEAR SYSTEM : 2
/ Scheme 14 is distributive/residual-distribution; keep linear FE to avoid
/ the TELEMAC stop: "DISTRIBUTIVE SCHEMES NOT IMPLEMENTED FOR QUASI-BULLE AND QUADRATIC ELEMENTS".
DISCRETIZATIONS IN SPACE : 11;11
SCHEME FOR ADVECTION OF VELOCITIES : 14
MAXIMUM NUMBER OF ITERATIONS FOR ADVECTION SCHEMES : 100
NUMBER OF SUB-ITERATIONS FOR NON-LINEARITIES : 2
IMPLICITATION FOR DEPTH : 0.80
IMPLICITATION FOR VELOCITY : 0.80
MASS-LUMPING ON H : 1.
MASS-LUMPING ON VELOCITY : 1.
SOLVER : 2
PRECONDITIONING : 2
SOLVER ACCURACY : 1e-05
MAXIMUM NUMBER OF ITERATIONS FOR SOLVER : 200
INFORMATION ABOUT SOLVER : YES
/
/ STABILITY CONTROLS
FREE SURFACE GRADIENT COMPATIBILITY : 0.9
CONTROL OF LIMITS : YES
LIMIT VALUES : -1000;9000;-1000;1000;-1000;1000;-1000;1000
/
/ TIDAL FLATS
TIDAL FLATS : YES
CONTINUITY CORRECTION : YES
OPTION FOR THE TREATMENT OF TIDAL FLATS : 1
TREATMENT OF NEGATIVE DEPTHS : 2
H CLIPPING : NO
/
/ BOUNDARY CONDITIONS
PRESCRIBED FLOWRATES : 0.;2.0000
PRESCRIBED ELEVATIONS : 329.240;0.
VELOCITY PROFILES : 1;4
OPTION FOR LIQUID BOUNDARIES : 1;1
/
/ FRICTION (zonal; coefficients calibrated by HydroBayesCal)
LAW OF BOTTOM FRICTION : 5
FRICTION COEFFICIENT : 0.07
LAW OF FRICTION ON LATERAL BOUNDARIES : 5
ROUGHNESS COEFFICIENT OF BOUNDARIES : 0.07
/
/ INITIAL CONDITIONS
/ pre-wetted warm start (channel seeded with water; see hydromate)
PREVIOUS COMPUTATION FILE : initial-conditions.slf
INITIAL TIME SET TO ZERO : YES
/
/ TURBULENCE (k-epsilon)
/ Existing turbulence model settings preserved.
DIFFUSION OF VELOCITY : YES
TURBULENCE MODEL : 3
ACCURACY OF K : 1e-06
ACCURACY OF EPSILON : 1e-06
/ Raise only the solve budget for the k-epsilon step; do not relax accuracies.
MAXIMUM NUMBER OF ITERATIONS FOR K AND EPSILON : 120
INFORMATION ABOUT K-EPSILON MODEL : YES
&FIN
